(6196166, 913597, 85430, '<td valign="top">i had a similar mid-day shot, and i found that the year-round overcast cloud in singapore seldom gives nice blue skies. i waited for sunset but this area faces south, and from your pov, the direction towards esplanade is east so at most i could get was some orange clouds, but no beautiful sunset. i waited till night and the lights under the bridge is an overpowering red that flood the entire shot taken at this angle. sometimes the light changes to very bright whites exploding even in the tiniest aperture. and the F1 night race lighting structures don''t add well to the composition. the surrounding areas are nice and really pretty for photographs, but for this challenge, you had to take a photo of the bridge that didn''t want to be photographed. Your photo was nicely done, and having known firsthand the level of difficulty involved in capturing this shot, plus the good overall technicals of this photo, i give you my high vote.</td>', 'i had a similar mid-day shot, and i found that the year-round overcast cloud in singapore seldom gives nice blue skies. i waited for sunset but this area faces south, and from your pov, the direction towards esplanade is east so at most i could get was some orange clouds, but no beautiful sunset. i waited till night and the lights under the bridge is an overpowering red that flood the entire shot taken at this angle. sometimes the light changes to very bright whites exploding even in the tiniest aperture. and the F1 night race lighting structures don''t add well to the composition. the surrounding areas are nice and really pretty for photographs, but for this challenge, you had to take a photo of the bridge that didn''t want to be photographed. Your photo was nicely done, and having known firsthand the level of difficulty involved in capturing this shot, plus the good overall technicals of this photo, i give you my high vote.', '2010-10-20 00:17:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6196177, 914325, 83313, '<td valign="top">I like the view, but the use of selective desat is not working for me, I''m afraid.</td>', 'I like the view, but the use of selective desat is not working for me, I''m afraid.', '2010-10-20 00:52:58.000000', NULL, 1),
