(6196687, 914083, 69324, '<td valign="top">Nice job representing the Pentax camp.</td>', 'Nice job representing the Pentax camp.', '2010-10-20 11:18:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(6196709, 914195, 108069, '<td valign="top">I agree with the last commenter. ; ) Nice shot, and really nice recap of some history. My only advice is that you guys need to stop naming your bridges after British military officers.</td>', 'I agree with the last commenter. ; ) Nice shot, and really nice recap of some history. My only advice is that you guys need to stop naming your bridges after British military officers.', '2010-10-20 11:46:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(6196719, 914307, 103142, '<td valign="top">I love this shot -- it was one of my 8s. The processing is wonderful. The sepia-type tones are great, but having the hints of greens make it incredible. I wouldn''t have thought of processing something like that, and I''m a loss on how you managed to do it. Did you actually tone the picture? Or was it simply creative desat/selective color? I would love to know -- it''s such a beautiful result.</td>', 'I love this shot -- it was one of my 8s. The processing is wonderful. The sepia-type tones are great, but having the hints of greens make it incredible. I wouldn''t have thought of processing something like that, and I''m a loss on how you managed to do it. Did you actually tone the picture? Or was it simply creative desat/selective color? I would love to know -- it''s such a beautiful result.', '2010-10-20 12:05:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6196732, 914093, 79955, '<td valign="top">Hi Enzo, excellent shot of the Henderson Waves. Sorry I missed on catching up with you. Next time around ok ?</td>', 'Hi Enzo, excellent shot of the Henderson Waves. Sorry I missed on catching up with you. Next time around ok ?', '2010-10-20 12:13:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(6196755, 913497, 59796, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the top 10. I believe this shot should''ve placed higher than it did. The picture is wonderfully balanced with the bridge support on the left and the rocks on the right. And the bridge itself seems to go on forever. The cloudy sky sets a wonderful mood (not too menacing like the other pic :). My only nit is that the horizon is neither centered nor at 1/3, so it''s noticeable and feels weird scanning the pic from top to bottom. Very well done.</td>', 'Congrats on the top 10. I believe this shot should''ve placed higher than it did. The picture is wonderfully balanced with the bridge support on the left and the rocks on the right. And the bridge itself seems to go on forever. The cloudy sky sets a wonderful mood (not too menacing like the other pic :). My only nit is that the horizon is neither centered nor at 1/3, so it''s noticeable and feels weird scanning the pic from top to bottom. Very well done.', '2010-10-20 12:20:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(6196778, 914041, 68020, '<td valign="top">congrats on the top ten...this was my top three favorites..</td>', 'congrats on the top ten...this was my top three favorites..', '2010-10-20 12:40:44.000000', NULL, 0),
