(6790560, 913956, 69008, '<td valign="top">This is a strange thing to see. The road bed was added to the old RR trestle left over from the Overseas Railway after the ''35 hurricane. They added structure above the RR and put the road surface on top of that.  It''s falling into the water now, a piece at a time. The "spalling" of the concrete is from the rebar rusting inside the concrete, because they mixed the concrete with salt water when the bridge was built. It makes the concrete pop open like that. <br/> This is a marvelous location for vacationing. It''s about 40 miles from Ke West and has a nice anchorage (anchored there before,) good campground and award winning beaches with beautiful water.</td>', 'This is a strange thing to see. The road bed was added to the old RR trestle left over from the Overseas Railway after the ''35 hurricane. They added structure above the RR and put the road surface on top of that.  It''s falling into the water now, a piece at a time. The "spalling" of the concrete is from the rebar rusting inside the concrete, because they mixed the concrete with salt water when the bridge was built. It makes the concrete pop open like that.  This is a marvelous location for vacationing. It''s about 40 miles from Ke West and has a nice anchorage (anchored there before,) good campground and award winning beaches with beautiful water.', '2012-06-08 13:51:15.000000', NULL, 0),
